original_source":{"page_or_item":"15 FR 5834, PDF pages 6-6; para. 1 (lead-in)","sha256":"12793b8c9d4822cbd216fa9d206cef28370695f2e51e04c459f9bc91c506b360","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1950-08-30/pdf/FR-1950-08-30.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:10157#para1","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) The employee shall have served \ncontinuously in a full-time, active-duty \nstatus in the competitive service, without \na break in service of more than sixty cal­\nendar days, during the two years im­\nmediately prior to the date of this order:  \nProvided, that military service shall not \nbe regarded as a break in service.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"15 FR 5834, PDF pages 6-6; para. 1(a)","sha256":"12793b8c9d4822cbd216fa9d206cef28370695f2e51e04c459f9bc91c506b360","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1950-08-30/pdf/FR-1950-08-30.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:10157#para1(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) If his employment is evaluated \nunder an efficiency rating system, the \nmost recent rating of the employee must \nbe “Good” or better, and if his employ­\nment is not so evaluated, the head of \nthe agency in which he is employed must \ncertify to the Civil Service Commission \nthat the employee has served with merit \nfor six months or longer immediately \nprior to the date of such certification.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"15 FR 5834, PDF pages 6-6; para. 1(b)","sha256":"12793b8c9d4822cbd216fa9d206cef28370695f2e51e04c459f9bc91c506b360","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1950-08-30/pdf/FR-1950-08-30.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:10157#para1(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) The acquisition of competitive \nstatus by the employee must be recom­\nmended by the head of the agency in \nwhich he is employed within six months \nof the date of this order.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"15 FR 5834, PDF pages 6-6; para. 1(c)","sha256":"12793b8c9d4822cbd216fa9d206cef28370695f2e51e04c459f9bc91c506b360","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1950-08-30/pdf/FR-1950-08-30.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:10157#para1(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(d) The employee must successfully \nqualify in such suitable noncompetitive \nexamination as the Civil Service Com­\nmission may prescribe: Provided, That \nonly one such noncompetitive examina­\ntion shall be given him.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"15 FR 5834, PDF pages 6-6; para. 1(d)","sha256":"12793b8c9d4822cbd216fa9d206cef28370695f2e51e04c459f9bc91c506b360","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1950-08-30/pdf/FR-1950-08-30.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:10157#para1(d)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"2. This order shall not be applicable to\n(a) postmasters; (b) rural carriers in \nthose cases with respect to which there \nis an existing register of eligibles for \nfilling the position In question or with \nrespect to which an examination has \nbeen announced by the Civil Service \nCommission for filling such position; and\n(c) persons not entitled to veteran pref­\nerence who are serving in positions \nwhich are by law or by Executive order \nrestricted to preference eligibles.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"15 FR 5834, PDF pages 6-6; para. 2","sha256":"12793b8c9d4822cbd216fa9d206cef28370695f2e51e04c459f9bc91c506b360","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1950-08-30/pdf/FR-1950-08-30.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:10157#para2","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"3. For the purposes of this order, em­\nployees who are on active military duty \non the date hereof shall be considered as \nbeing in an active-duty status.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"15 FR 5834, PDF pages 6-6; para. 3","sha256":"12793b8c9d4822cbd216fa9d206cef28370695f2e51e04c459f9bc91c506b360","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1950-08-30/pdf/FR-1950-08-30.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:10157#para3","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"4. The Civil Service Commission shall \npromulgate regulations to effectuate the \npurposes of this order.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"15 FR 5834, PDF pages 6-6; para. 4","sha256":"12793b8c9d4822cbd216fa9d206cef28370695f2e51e04c459f9bc91c506b360","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1950-08-30/pdf/FR-1950-08-30.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:10157#para4","state_at_cutoff":null}],"original_representation":{"page_or_item":"15 FR 5834, PDF pages 6-6","sha256":"12793b8c9d4822cbd216fa9d206cef28370695f2e51e04c459f9bc91c506b360","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1950-08-30/pdf/FR-1950-08-30.pdf"},"research_rationale":"","savings_residuals":null,"schema":"eo-lifecycle-claim/v1","unresolved_material_gaps":["DRAFT: state_at_cutoff not decided for 8 clause(s); clause inventory completeness not confirmed","DRAFT: whole-order ending not established","DRAFT: savings and residual effects not closed","DRAFT: later_source_search not recorded (machine searches are proposals only; paste them after judging them adequate and resolving every CONFLICT line)"],"whole_order_end":null,"whole_order_status":"no"},"draft_schema":"eo-claim-draft/v1","instrument_id":"EO:10157"}
